\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\li792\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.4.\tab Record Storage and Security \par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj\b0 4.4.1.\tab Deputy analysts enter the data into the computer software / databases.\par
4.4.2.\tab It is the rABConsibility of Deputy Analyst to keep the entire testing related data password protected and only Analyst can access the data.\par
4.4.3.\tab Only LMSC / Analyst & Deputy analysts have access to make any changes in the data being kept.\par
4.4.4.\tab Records of all these changes will be kept and changes will be highlighted.\par
4.4.5.\tab Data is only be transmitted through emails and the records of such emails will be maintained.\par
4.4.6.\tab Deputy Analysts are also rABConsible to take the periodic data backups i.e. once per month minimum.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\li792\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.5.\tab Amendment in Records\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj\b0 4.5.1.\tab Physical records (on paper) can be amended for correction of spelling or grammatical errors by striking out the incorrect portion with a single line as this \ldblquote\strike this is incorrect\strike0\rdblquote , and entering the correct word alongside with initials of the authoritative person.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\tab Note: This also applies to data that is entered on registers.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.5.2.\tab In case a Physical record expresses error in values of test results (e.g. an incorrect test report), it is reprinted / reproduced with renewed identification. Previous record is marked as obsolete and stored with obsolete records.\par
4.5.3.\tab Records kept in electronic form are amended after authorization by concerned officials, while making sure that incorrect version is backed up in a separate folder.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\li792\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.6.\tab File Management\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\b0 ABCAK Lab has established a filing system to manage and control all the files, folders and registers being maintained which provides the details about uniquely identifying and file labeling.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.6.1.\tab File/Folder/Register Coding System\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj All files, folders and registers will have a unique identification code according to this scheme;\par
\tab\tab\b\ldblquote ABC-LAB- FIL-NNN\rdblquote\par
